dsl:
title: The geometric law has no memory
problem: After s failures, the number of further failures has the same law as at the start.
param p = 0.2 "success probability of each trial"
param s = 5 {failures}
param t = 3 {failures}
X ~ geometric(p = p) {failures}
ratio memory = E[X >= s + t] / E[X >= s] "P(X ≥ s + t | X ≥ s)"
prob fresh = X >= t "P(X ≥ t)"
focus X

title: Spare seals for a remote pump station
problem: Pump seals fail at random times. The station gets new parts every 8 weeks. Find the number of spare seals to keep.
param rate = 0.3 {faults per week}
param weeks = 8 {weeks}
param stock = 5 {seals}
param hold = 2 {currency units} "holding cost of one unused seal"
param short = 50 {currency units} "cost of one seal that is not available"
D ~ poisson(lambda = rate*weeks) {seals needed}
prob stockout = D > stock "more faults than spare seals"
mean cost = hold*max(stock - D, 0) + short*max(D - stock, 0) {currency units per period}
alt "3 seals": stock = 3
alt "5 seals": stock = 5
alt "7 seals": stock = 7
minimise cost
require stockout <= 0.05
focus D
